## 4. Binding architectural constraints

| # | Constraint | Rationale |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| A1 | ${SSOT_NAME} is the SSoT | Coherence, security, evolvability |
| A2 | This repo communicates with ${SSOT_NAME} only via the typed boundary client | No raw access |
| A3 | Schema-driven boundary (one canonical schema language) | End-to-end typing, no drift |
| A4 | Authorization is server-side; UI is cosmetic | Security cannot be delegated to the client |
| A5 | All mutations carry `Idempotency-Key` | Safe retries |
| A6 | Long-running operations are first-class `Job` | Non-blocking UX, audit, retry |
| A7 | Time in UTC; geo in canonical format | Coherence |
| A8 | Audit mandatory for sensitive actions | Compliance, debugging |
| A9 | No secrets in the client | Anti-leak |
| A10 | Forward-compatible schemas (`X-Schema-Version`) | Decoupled deploys |
| A11 | Versioned config/policy with rollback | Reversibility |
| A12 | <project-specific constraint> | <reason> |

